diff --git a/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5 b/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5
index 9fe5ac2..02cfea9 100644
--- a/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5
+++ b/doc/man/man5/slurm.conf.5
@@ -4470,6 +4470,21 @@ Enable job steps that span heterogeneous job allocations.
 The default value.
 .IP
 
+.TP
+\fBhet_component_node_fail\fR
+When a node fails, only the heterogeneous job component that holds the node is
+affected: it loses the node (\-\-no\-kill) or ends with NODE_FAIL. The other
+components are neither resized nor killed. A component other than the leader
+is not requeued alone, since the batch script runs on the leader. The exception
+is the leader itself: if it holds the failed node and cannot continue without
+it, or the node runs its batch script (even with \-\-no\-kill), the whole
+heterogeneous job takes the failure: every component is requeued if it can be,
+and otherwise ends with NODE_FAIL, with or without \-\-no\-kill.
+Components of jobs submitted with \fBsbatch \-\-het\-batch=each\fR always fail
+independently, and can be requeued alone.
+By default, a node failure affects every component of the heterogeneous job.
+.IP
+
 .TP
 \fBenable_job_state_cache\fR
 Enables an independent cache of job state details within slurmctld. This allows
